Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/turnip: align automatic A640 VM_BIND allocations to 64 KiB

Mesa 26.2.4 on RMX1931 / A640 can fault on a CCU read before a
page-aligned UBWC color BO during a GMEM resolve. A Vulkan regression
that frees the preceding small allocations reproduces the fault in its
first draw. The fault is 8 KiB before the color mapping, at its base
rounded down to 64 KiB; the page-table entry is zero. Leaving preceding
mappings present or selecting sysmem avoids the fault.

Match the existing A640 kernel-managed VM alignment for automatically
allocated userspace VM_BIND addresses. Keep mapping lengths, explicit
capture/replay addresses, sparse offsets, legacy allocation and other
GPU models unchanged.

The same-build baseline and the installed Mesa library both reproduce
the failure. The aligned candidate passes hole, MSAA and format/size
pixel regressions. See reference/kernel149 for deployment and receipts.

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm.cc
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_drm.cc
@@ -23,6 +23,15 @@
 {
    *iova = 0;
 
+   /* Match the A640 kernel-managed address alignment for automatic VM_BIND
+    * allocations. Mapping sizes and explicit capture/replay addresses retain
+    * their original granularity.
+    */
+   uint64_t alignment = os_page_size;
+   if (dev->physical_device->has_vm_bind &&
+       dev->physical_device->dev_id.gpu_id == 640)
+      alignment = MAX2(alignment, UINT64_C(0x10000));
+
    if (flags & TU_BO_ALLOC_REPLAYABLE) {
       if (client_iova) {
          if (util_vma_heap_alloc_addr(&dev->vma, client_iova, size)) {
@@ -36,11 +45,11 @@
           * them from the other end of the address space.
           */
          dev->vma.alloc_high = true;
-         *iova = util_vma_heap_alloc(&dev->vma, size, os_page_size);
+         *iova = util_vma_heap_alloc(&dev->vma, size, alignment);
       }
    } else {
       dev->vma.alloc_high = false;
-      *iova = util_vma_heap_alloc(&dev->vma, size, os_page_size);
+      *iova = util_vma_heap_alloc(&dev->vma, size, alignment);
    }
 
    if (!*iova)
